From a88b5d6f47e73df7d819b2661745bc1c854560e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cheng Fangming <chengfangming1993@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 23:08:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] media: iris: bound legacy VPU5 aggregate load

Keep the maximum clock and interconnect votes stable while legacy VPU5 is powered, and only cache successful runtime vote changes.

Reserve aggregate macroblocks per second before CAPTURE allocation so workloads beyond the SM8150 4K120 decode budget fail cleanly before the firmware exhausts its VBUF pool. Estimate decoder rate from queued timestamps, retain 8K30 admission, release reservations on teardown, and suppress repeated userspace REQBUFS rejection logs.
---
